705 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Logo Clear Space\n\n\nTo ensure the logo remains clear\054 recognizable\054 and visually balanced\054 a protective clear space must always be maintained around it\056 This area prevents other graphic elements\054 text\054 images\054 or layout borders from interfering with the logo\056\n\nThe minimum clear space is defined by the height and width of the letter \034P\035 from the logo typography\056 This spacing should be applied equally on all sides of the logo and must remain free from any additional visual elements\056 Maintaining this rule helps preserve brand consistency\054 readability\054 and a professional appearance across all applications\056)
     /K [ 0 ]
     /P 706 0 R
     /Pg 678 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

